  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting the Global Economic Change Oxfam America program and Oxfam International&#x2019;s GINI work, these efforts in Vietnam aim to:
&#x2022;Mainstream and inspire new narratives of a transformative future for Vietnam into public discussions.
&#x2022; Update Vietnam&#x2019;s inequalityevidence, insights, and documented innovations to highlight improvements, identify persisting inequalities, and uncover new areas of disparity that require innovative policy interventions, and
&#x2022; Engage strategic policymakers at national and subnational levels through data, reports, and communication to inspire the stronger adoption of the updated Human Economy framework.
More details available in this concept note: https://oxfam.box.com/s/a3o96a0e8rdmka5d7hatk578dwwobbt8</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM USA</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Vietnam , Oxfam is one of the leading international, non -governmental organisation. Since 1955, Oxfam is active in Vietnam withhumanitarian interventions and started development work in the late 1980&apos;s. Today, Oxfam works in 26 provinces with people, governments and civil society to promote equality and well-being through social and economic change.</narrative>
